Panel chrome for the beamenu launcher.

Adds bm_menu_set_search_height(): in rich mode the query line gets a height of
its own rather than sharing the list row height, and a hairline in the border
colour separates it from the results. Together with bemenu's existing --center,
--radius, --fixed-height and --width-factor this is the whole Raycast panel
shape; nothing here changes classic (non-rich) rendering.

diff --git a/lib/bemenu.h b/lib/bemenu.h
index 623f36c..b766c0a 100644
--- a/lib/bemenu.h
+++ b/lib/bemenu.h
@@ -635,6 +635,27 @@ BM_PUBLIC void bm_menu_set_icon_size(struct bm_menu *menu, uint32_t icon_size);
  */
 BM_PUBLIC uint32_t bm_menu_get_icon_size(struct bm_menu *menu);
 
+/**
+ * Set the height of the search row in the rich layout.
+ *
+ * A launcher panel reads better when the query line is taller than the rows
+ * under it. Only honoured when the rich layout is enabled; 0 keeps the search
+ * row the same height as a list row. A hairline in the border colour is drawn
+ * between the search row and the list whenever this is non-zero.
+ *
+ * @param menu bm_menu instance where to set the search row height.
+ * @param search_height 0 to match the list row height, > 0 for that many pixels.
+ */
+BM_PUBLIC void bm_menu_set_search_height(struct bm_menu *menu, uint32_t search_height);
+
+/**
+ * Get the height of the search row in the rich layout.
+ *
+ * @param menu bm_menu instance to query.
+ * @return uint32_t search row height in pixels, 0 when matching list rows.
+ */
+BM_PUBLIC uint32_t bm_menu_get_search_height(struct bm_menu *menu);
+
 /**
  * Set height of cursor in pixels.
  * Some renderers such as ncurses may ignore this when it does not make sense.
diff --git a/lib/internal.h b/lib/internal.h
